Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.057
Visal, how was your internship?

68
00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:08.123
Great! By the time I finished the internship, I had learned valuable skills.

69
00:04:09.217 --> 00:04:10.775
Had you worked before?

70
00:04:11.883 --> 00:04:16.985
No, I had never worked in an office before. I was nervous at first.

71
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:19.073
What helped?

72
00:04:20.183 --> 00:04:25.422
My supervisor had prepared a clear plan, so I knew what to do.

73
00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.485
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:32.754
Grammar focus: Past perfect for prior experience.

75
00:04:33.054 --> 00:04:34.276
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:34.983 --> 00:04:38.980
By the time I finished the internship, I had learned valuable skills.

77
00:04:39.883 --> 00:04:42.510
I had never worked in an office before that summer.

78
00:04:43.417 --> 00:04:46.333
When I arrived, my supervisor had prepared a plan.

79
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:53.282
Use the past perfect (had + past participle) for the action that happened first, before another past action.

80
00:04:54.017 --> 00:04:58.573
Be careful! Don't say: By the time I finished, I learned have skills.

81
00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:03.740
Say: By the time I finished, I had learned skills.

82
00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.143
The past perfect is 'had' + past participle.

83
